WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.123
- I'm an American.

00:00:02.123 --> 00:00:05.110
Please you have to believe
me, this is a mistake.

00:00:05.110 --> 00:00:05.943
Sir?

00:00:05.943 --> 00:00:06.776
- Come on now.

00:00:06.776 --> 00:00:07.695
It's not up to me.

00:00:07.695 --> 00:00:12.695
♪ Small pale house ♪

00:00:15.270 --> 00:00:19.437
♪ A moment's march from the beach ♪

00:00:28.932 --> 00:00:33.932
♪ My day is growing near ♪

00:00:44.053 --> 00:00:49.053
♪ And here I find no peace at all ♪

00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:02.044
- Here they are.

00:01:02.044 --> 00:01:04.070
(ominous music)

00:01:04.070 --> 00:01:05.420
- It's so quiet.

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:08.373
- They are much more
docile compared to Max.

00:01:09.340 --> 00:01:10.910
Our red uniforms are for our level two,

00:01:10.910 --> 00:01:13.140
people with felony convictions, etc.

00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:16.480
Orange are our level
one's, our non-criminals.

00:01:16.480 --> 00:01:19.091
- So they're in orange,
but they aren't criminals?

00:01:19.091 --> 00:01:21.323
- Well, they are criminals.

00:01:21.323 --> 00:01:23.120
They're here, right?

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:24.870
They came to our country illegally.

00:01:24.870 --> 00:01:26.840
- That's exactly right, Carlos.

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:29.620
Carlos Lupa, Natalie
Figueroa our new warden.

00:01:29.620 --> 00:01:32.670
Mr. Lupa is head of ICE
here at PolyCon detention.

00:01:32.670 --> 00:01:35.180
ICE handles the processing,
the legal, the deportation,

00:01:35.180 --> 00:01:36.536
and PolyCon handles the
housing and feeding.

00:01:36.536 --> 00:01:39.780
(wings flapping)

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:41.750
- What's with the bird?

00:01:41.750 --> 00:01:43.480
- Cute, right?

00:01:43.480 --> 00:01:45.460
Flew in here a few days ago.

00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:46.710
- Keeps the ladies entertained,

00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:49.510
so we decided not to deport it. (laughs)

00:01:49.510 --> 00:01:52.140
- Do any of them speak English?

00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:55.557
- Some, though, most favor
(speaking foreign language).

00:01:56.580 --> 00:01:58.190
Majority here are from Mexico,

00:01:58.190 --> 00:02:02.140
followed by El Salvador,
Honduras, Guatemala.

00:02:02.140 --> 00:02:03.510
Then we have your others:

00:02:03.510 --> 00:02:07.960
your Haitians, your
Jamaicans, general Africans.

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:11.420
Of course there's your Asian
nerds, your cool Asians

00:02:11.420 --> 00:02:12.963
but beware of the Plastics.

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:16.320
That was a "Mean Girls" joke.

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:19.890
- So, it's like the
It's a Small World ride,

00:02:19.890 --> 00:02:22.480
but minus the joy and the singing,

00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:25.260
and the line is just as long.

00:02:25.260 --> 00:02:28.420
- Some do-gooder, lawyer-advocate
types told the detainees

00:02:28.420 --> 00:02:29.530
who were working in the kitchen

00:02:29.530 --> 00:02:32.200
that they don't get paid, and
it doesn't help their case

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:34.220
so they quit.

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:36.430
- Looks like you have your first task.

00:02:36.430 --> 00:02:38.320
Luckily, America's cheapest labor forces

00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:39.470
are just down the hill.

00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:50.410
- I need to get in touch with someone

00:02:50.410 --> 00:02:53.333
so that I can prove that I was born here.

00:02:55.340 --> 00:02:56.577
I'm gonna ask for my phone call.

00:02:56.577 --> 00:02:58.027
- You don't get a phone call.

00:02:59.837 --> 00:03:01.900
- (scoffs) But there
are phones right there.

00:03:01.900 --> 00:03:03.423
- You don't get a free call.

00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:06.300
You gotta pay to set up an account.

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:08.110
You gotta pay per minute.

00:03:08.110 --> 00:03:10.820
- Okay well fuck that, when
I get assigned my lawyer,

00:03:10.820 --> 00:03:12.007
that's the first thing I'm gonna do.

00:03:12.007 --> 00:03:14.173
- You don't get a lawyer.

00:03:14.173 --> 00:03:15.633
- (Scoffs) What?

00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:18.250
This is America.

00:03:18.250 --> 00:03:19.083
- Not in here.

00:03:21.259 --> 00:03:25.009
(speaks in foreign language)

00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:34.450
- Touch me again,

00:03:34.450 --> 00:03:36.090
and you're going in the box.

00:03:36.090 --> 00:03:39.544
And you need to speak English or Spanish,

00:03:39.544 --> 00:03:43.294
(speaking foreign language)?

00:03:45.682 --> 00:03:47.287
- Oh my God, oh my God!

00:03:49.240 --> 00:03:50.073
- Hey, excuse me.

00:03:50.073 --> 00:03:51.450
Do not touch the inmate, immigrant.

00:03:51.450 --> 00:03:52.700
Do not touch the immigrant.

00:03:52.700 --> 00:03:53.680
- Why don't you take it over there?

00:03:53.680 --> 00:03:54.513
We got this.

00:03:56.038 --> 00:03:57.240
- Oh my God, girl, am I tripping?

00:03:57.240 --> 00:03:59.500
I thought I'd never see you again.

00:03:59.500 --> 00:04:01.010
Girl, you look hot.

00:04:01.010 --> 00:04:03.060
- Well duh, I'm still me.

00:04:03.060 --> 00:04:05.134
- No, I mean sweaty.

00:04:05.134 --> 00:04:08.040
- Oh, it's like a fucking
dank-ass locker room in here.

00:04:08.040 --> 00:04:09.222
It's the worst.

00:04:09.222 --> 00:04:10.630
Flaca, you have no idea.

00:04:10.630 --> 00:04:11.820
You have to help me get out.

00:04:11.820 --> 00:04:12.860
- What do you mean?

00:04:12.860 --> 00:04:14.033
Help you escape?

00:04:14.033 --> 00:04:16.090
- No, no, it's a mistake that I'm here.

00:04:16.090 --> 00:04:17.270
I need you to find my mom.

00:04:17.270 --> 00:04:18.740
Tell her, I know she's mad at me,

00:04:18.740 --> 00:04:19.955
but that this is an emergency, okay?

00:04:19.955 --> 00:04:20.788
Maria Ramos in Miami.

00:04:20.788 --> 00:04:22.590
- Okay, don't worry, okay.

00:04:22.590 --> 00:04:24.770
Worry face gives you
elevens between your brows.

00:04:24.770 --> 00:04:25.603
- Okay.
- I got you.

00:04:25.603 --> 00:04:26.436
- Okay.

00:04:29.114 --> 00:04:32.280
(hysterical crying)

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:33.310
- What happened to her?

00:04:33.310 --> 00:04:35.570
- Patient presented with
severe abdominal upset

00:04:35.570 --> 00:04:36.660
and vaginal spotting,

00:04:36.660 --> 00:04:38.840
and thankfully the
pregnancy is still viable.

00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:39.999
- She's pregnant?

00:04:39.999 --> 00:04:41.270
(speaking in foreign language)

00:04:41.270 --> 00:04:42.920
- I'd say about nine weeks along.

00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:44.370
- So, why is she still screaming?

00:04:44.370 --> 00:04:45.300
- She's scared.

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:46.133
Poor thing, she doesn't know

00:04:46.133 --> 00:04:48.272
that her little hugywugy is gonna be okay.

00:04:48.272 --> 00:04:51.200
Mama, your baby is gonna be okay.

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:52.776
Your baby's gonna be okay.

00:04:52.776 --> 00:04:56.620
(yells in foreign language)

00:04:56.620 --> 00:04:58.380
- Where is her translator?

00:04:58.380 --> 00:04:59.960
- We don't have a translator for that.

00:04:59.960 --> 00:05:01.970
- You're suppose to file a report

00:05:01.970 --> 00:05:04.127
if a detainee needs the language line.

00:05:04.127 --> 00:05:06.040
- I have a new courtroom to oversee,

00:05:06.040 --> 00:05:08.521
so it sounds like a you problem to me.

00:05:08.521 --> 00:05:12.227
(somber piano music)

00:05:12.227 --> 00:05:15.810
(begs in foreign language)

00:05:20.515 --> 00:05:22.370
(phone rings)

00:05:22.370 --> 00:05:23.600
- [Maria] Hello?

00:05:23.600 --> 00:05:25.459
- Do you know Maritza Ramos?

00:05:25.459 --> 00:05:26.960
- [Maria] Yes.

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:28.170
- Really?

00:05:28.170 --> 00:05:31.610
Oh my God, are you the
Maria Ramos, Maritza's mom?

00:05:31.610 --> 00:05:33.000
- Yes, what's going on?

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:34.870
- Hi, I'm her best friend, Flaca

00:05:34.870 --> 00:05:36.330
and I know you wouldn't take her calls

00:05:36.330 --> 00:05:37.200
when she got out of prison,

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:39.620
but this is an emergency, so please.

00:05:39.620 --> 00:05:40.780
- Is Maritza okay?

00:05:40.780 --> 00:05:42.600
- No, she's in immigration prison,

00:05:42.600 --> 00:05:44.730
because she doesn't have her ID.

00:05:44.730 --> 00:05:46.890
She needs her US birth
certificate to prove

00:05:46.890 --> 00:05:48.611
that she's a citizen.

00:05:48.611 --> 00:05:51.220
(Maria sighs)

00:05:51.220 --> 00:05:52.440
- I don't have it.

00:05:52.440 --> 00:05:55.370
- Okay, well, can you
go to the record place,

00:05:55.370 --> 00:05:56.670
and get her a replacement?

00:05:59.020 --> 00:06:01.733
- No, what I'm saying is there isn't one.

00:06:02.940 --> 00:06:04.304
Maritza wasn't born here.

00:06:04.304 --> 00:06:07.304
(suspenseful music)

00:06:10.960 --> 00:06:13.660
- State your true and complete name.

00:06:13.660 --> 00:06:15.650
- Karla Diana Adelena Cordova.

00:06:15.650 --> 00:06:17.760
- At your last proceeding,
your case was set over

00:06:17.760 --> 00:06:19.600
to give you time to find an attorney,

00:06:19.600 --> 00:06:21.430
yet you're here today without an attorney.

00:06:21.430 --> 00:06:23.660
- I'm representing myself, your honor.

00:06:23.660 --> 00:06:25.790
I'd like to file my application for relief

00:06:25.790 --> 00:06:28.070
under the Convention Against Torture act.

00:06:28.070 --> 00:06:31.610
- Do you have a filled
out I589 application

00:06:31.610 --> 00:06:33.440
and your supporting evidence

00:06:33.440 --> 00:06:35.050
that demonstrate you will be tortured

00:06:35.050 --> 00:06:36.780
if returned to El Salvador today?

00:06:36.780 --> 00:06:37.730
- I do, your honor.

00:06:42.150 --> 00:06:44.790
The newspaper article is about the school

00:06:44.790 --> 00:06:46.490
where I used to teach and I lived.

00:06:46.490 --> 00:06:49.800
The year that I left, we had 36 deaths.

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:52.850
All of them boys who
refused to join gangs.

00:06:52.850 --> 00:06:54.370
I knew them all personally,

00:06:54.370 --> 00:06:56.100
many of them were my students.

00:06:56.100 --> 00:06:58.550
They were good boys,
but they had no way out.

00:06:58.550 --> 00:06:59.530
When I became pregnant,

00:06:59.530 --> 00:07:02.470
my husband and I knew we had to leave.

00:07:02.470 --> 00:07:04.170
We couldn't risk our child's life.

00:07:04.170 --> 00:07:06.820
- Gang violence is not grounds for CAT.

00:07:06.820 --> 00:07:08.270
It's not even grounds for asylum.

00:07:08.270 --> 00:07:09.103
- I'm getting to that.

00:07:09.103 --> 00:07:10.370
- Speed it up, Ms. Cardova.

00:07:10.370 --> 00:07:13.600
- I have two boys now, American boys.

00:07:13.600 --> 00:07:15.500
I can't take them to a country

00:07:15.500 --> 00:07:19.000
where their choices are kill or be killed.

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:21.450
The Convention Against
Torture clearly states

00:07:21.450 --> 00:07:24.480
that torture is intense suffering

00:07:24.480 --> 00:07:28.120
that is inflicted in order
to obtain information

00:07:28.120 --> 00:07:29.898
or to coerce.

00:07:29.898 --> 00:07:31.890
(scoffs) If I take my boys back,

00:07:31.890 --> 00:07:34.320
they'll be coerced into join in the gangs,

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:37.590
or they will suffer the consequences.

00:07:37.590 --> 00:07:39.640
The very definition by which CAT stands.

00:07:39.640 --> 00:07:42.860
- The state is not deporting
Ms. Cordova's kids.

00:07:42.860 --> 00:07:44.680
The state is deporting Ms. Cordova.

00:07:44.680 --> 00:07:46.070
- I'm not leaving them.

00:07:46.070 --> 00:07:47.810
Their father passed away last year,

00:07:47.810 --> 00:07:48.910
I'm all they have.

00:07:48.910 --> 00:07:50.850
- Your honor, Ms. Cordova
doesn't even have custody

00:07:50.850 --> 00:07:51.683
of her children.

00:07:51.683 --> 00:07:52.810
- That's only because I'm in here.

00:07:52.810 --> 00:07:54.940
- I'm seeing your children
are already placed

00:07:54.940 --> 00:07:56.630
in pre-adoptive foster care.

00:07:56.630 --> 00:07:59.620
- I'm their mother, I will
file to get them back.

00:07:59.620 --> 00:08:02.160
- Ms. Cordova, your
children will be safer here.

00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:04.390
If anyone's made that case, it's you.

00:08:04.390 --> 00:08:06.300
Unfortunately, what you have failed to do

00:08:06.300 --> 00:08:07.930
is make a case for yourself.

00:08:07.930 --> 00:08:10.960
This application doesn't
even make a prima facie case

00:08:10.960 --> 00:08:12.740
for relief under the CAT.

00:08:12.740 --> 00:08:14.340
I'm denying your case,

00:08:14.340 --> 00:08:17.786
and I am issuing a
written order of removal.

00:08:17.786 --> 00:08:21.229
- You can't! (sobs)

00:08:21.229 --> 00:08:23.728
(sobbing) No.

00:08:23.728 --> 00:08:26.895
(intense piano music)

00:08:30.435 --> 00:08:33.210
(baby cries)

00:08:33.210 --> 00:08:34.510
- Good afternoon, ladies and gentlemen.

00:08:34.510 --> 00:08:36.650
My name is Judge Christine Holister,

00:08:36.650 --> 00:08:39.890
and we're sitting in Immigration
court in Lichfeild, NY.

00:08:39.890 --> 00:08:41.480
These are removal proceedings

00:08:41.480 --> 00:08:44.180
for siblings Alma and Santiago Casillas.

00:08:44.180 --> 00:08:47.000
Let the records show the
respondents are present in court

00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:48.230
but without an attorney.

00:08:48.230 --> 00:08:51.193
Do you understand what
these proceedings are about?

00:08:52.050 --> 00:08:54.893
Ms. Casillas, do you and
your brother have a lawyer?

00:08:56.960 --> 00:08:58.698
Do you know what a lawyer is?

00:08:58.698 --> 00:08:59.531
- No.

00:09:00.890 --> 00:09:03.300
- Well do you understand that we are here

00:09:03.300 --> 00:09:05.110
to determine whether or not

00:09:05.110 --> 00:09:07.574
you two can remain in the United States?

00:09:07.574 --> 00:09:09.630
- Can I used the bathroom?

00:09:09.630 --> 00:09:13.400
- I thought this courtroom
was for adult hearings?

00:09:13.400 --> 00:09:16.060
- We have a juvenile docket on Fridays.

00:09:16.060 --> 00:09:18.840
Illegal is an illegal,
even if they're mini.

00:09:18.840 --> 00:09:20.850
- And a piece of shit is a piece of shit

00:09:20.850 --> 00:09:21.813
even if he's grown.

00:09:22.660 --> 00:09:23.983
- She said shit.

00:09:23.983 --> 00:09:25.573
(children laughing)

00:09:25.573 --> 00:09:26.406
- Hey!

00:09:27.330 --> 00:09:28.775
- [Older Son] Mama?

00:09:28.775 --> 00:09:29.608
- Mijo?

00:09:29.608 --> 00:09:30.441
- Where are you?

00:09:30.441 --> 00:09:33.940
- Momma, they took our
cat and my Pokemon cards.

00:09:33.940 --> 00:09:35.683
- [Older Son] When are you coming back?

00:09:37.540 --> 00:09:40.403
- I'm working real hard on
getting back to you, okay?

00:09:42.350 --> 00:09:45.312
I'm going to be away for a little while,

00:09:45.312 --> 00:09:46.543
but I'm coming back.

00:09:46.543 --> 00:09:47.453
- But, when?

00:09:49.645 --> 00:09:51.290
- I don't know yet, but soon.

00:09:51.290 --> 00:09:54.580
You have to know that
no matter what happens,

00:09:54.580 --> 00:09:57.100
no matter what anyone tells you,

00:09:57.100 --> 00:10:00.753
I will not stop until
we're together again.

00:10:02.890 --> 00:10:05.063
- Will you be here for my birthday?

00:10:11.850 --> 00:10:13.810
- If I'm not, it just means

00:10:13.810 --> 00:10:17.203
that I'm still on my way, okay?

00:10:18.830 --> 00:10:20.430
It might take me a little while.

00:10:21.950 --> 00:10:24.930
So until then, you two need
to take care of each other,

00:10:24.930 --> 00:10:29.930
remind each other to drink
water and zip up your jackets.

00:10:30.102 --> 00:10:32.720
And you know how when you were little

00:10:33.600 --> 00:10:37.780
and you'd get real angry or sad,

00:10:37.780 --> 00:10:41.250
we used to talk about using your words.

00:10:41.250 --> 00:10:43.430
Well, you're gonna have to do that.

00:10:43.430 --> 00:10:46.823
You're gonna have to tell
people what you need.

00:10:48.500 --> 00:10:50.960
If there's something you don't understand

00:10:50.960 --> 00:10:55.023
or if something hurts,

00:10:58.010 --> 00:10:59.413
or if someone hurts you,

00:11:01.900 --> 00:11:04.220
you're gonna need to
speak up for yourselves

00:11:05.680 --> 00:11:08.040
and for each other,
because I won't be there

00:11:08.040 --> 00:11:09.267
to do it for you.

00:11:11.344 --> 00:11:12.227
(sniffles)

00:11:12.227 --> 00:11:14.937
I love you both more than anything.

00:11:17.187 --> 00:11:19.937
Never forget how much I love you.

00:11:23.716 --> 00:11:26.883
(somber guitar music)

00:11:41.371 --> 00:11:45.204
(singing in foreign language)

00:13:15.286 --> 00:13:19.248
♪ America, America ♪

00:13:19.248 --> 00:13:23.336
♪ We're all, we're all America ♪

00:13:23.336 --> 00:13:28.336
♪ America, America ♪

00:13:28.383 --> 00:13:33.383
♪ A home for you and me ♪

00:13:34.445 --> 00:13:39.445
♪ A home for you and me ♪

